<title>USA: N.Y. business loans rose $508 mln in April 2 wk.</title>
<headline>N.Y. business loans rose $508 mln in April 2 wk.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commercial and industrial loans at the six major New York banks, excluding acceptances, rose $508 million to $45,847 billion in the week ended April 2, the Federal Reserve Bank of New York said.</p>
<p>Including acceptances, loans rose $520 million to $46,121 billion.</p>
<p>Commercial paper outstanding nationally rose $3,976 billion to $838,429 billion.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
</text>
